Well, you will have to get the candles.

What follows is only a rough sketch of the proceeding of the game. In order
not to destroy all your fun, I will leave out the details:

The monster you killed to get the Orb (either the Orb of Detection or the
Orb of Fate) also carried a silver bell. This bell is one of the three keys
to the game. The other two are found later in the game. When having gotten
all three you'll have to do something at some place deep, deep down, almost
at the last level of the game. To provide for some special hints, I shall
quote the Oracle:

"It is said that thou mayst gain entry to Moloch's sanctuary, if thou
darest, from a place where the ground vibrates in the deepest depths of
Gehennom.  Thou needs must have the aid of three magical items.  The
pure sound of a silver bell shall announce thee.  The terrible runes,
read from Moloch's book, shall cause the earth to tremble mightily.  The
light of an enchanted candelabrum shall show thee the way."

Then you'll have to rip the Most Sacred Of All Amulets from the fangs
of Moloch and to return it to your god. To archieve the latter, now your
way is up right to the beginning of the game. Then, with The Amulet in
your hand, leave the dungeon. If you're still alive, you'll be near the
goal!!! You'll have to make your way through four worlds, dedicated to
the four forces of Earth, Air, Fire and Water. After that you will arrive
in Heaven (or Astra, as the ancient Greek called it). There you have to
return the Amulet to you God by sacrificing it on His High Temple.

You will then ascend to the State Of Demigodhood and go down in the 
Hall Of Fame as a Hero among Heroes.

